<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Part 1: Warm-up =
&amp; Introduction</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Go=
od morning Alex! Thanks for joining us today. I'm Sarah, Principal Engineer=
 here at NAB. I've been with the company for about 8 years now, primarily w=
orking on our digital banking platform architecture. Before we dive into th=
e technical deep dive, could you tell me a bit about your background and wh=
at excites you about frontend engineering?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Good=
 morning Sarah! Thanks for having me. I'm Alex, and I've been working as a =
frontend engineer for about 6 years now. My most recent role was as a Senio=
r Frontend Engineer at a fintech startup where I led the development of a t=
rading platform handling millions of transactions daily. What really excite=
s me about frontend engineering is the intersection of <strong>performance =
optimization</strong> and <strong>user experience</strong>. I'm particularl=
y passionate about understanding how JavaScript engines work under the hood=
 because it directly impacts how we write efficient, scalable code.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">In my current role, I've spent c=
onsiderable time optimizing React applications, working with state manageme=
nt libraries like Redux and Zustand, and implementing performance monitorin=
g solutions. I've also contributed to open-source projects related to <stro=
ng>bundler optimizations</strong> and <strong>memory profiling tools</stron=
g>.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Th=
at's great to hear! The performance aspect is crucial at NAB given our scal=
e. I noticed you mentioned understanding JavaScript engines - that's actual=
ly perfect for today's discussion. At NAB, we handle enormous volumes of da=
ta and user interactions, so <strong>engine-level optimizations</strong> be=
come critical.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Before we go deeper, I'm curious=
 - in your fintech experience, what were some of the biggest performance ch=
allenges you encountered, and how did understanding JavaScript internals he=
lp you solve them?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Exce=
llent question! One of the most significant challenges we faced was <strong=
>memory leaks in our real-time trading dashboard</strong>. We had thousands=
 of active WebSocket connections, real-time price updates, and complex stat=
e management. Users would leave the application open for hours, and we noti=
ced memory usage would gradually increase until the browser tab became unre=
sponsive.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The breakthrough came when I sta=
rted profiling with Chrome DevTools and discovered that we had <strong>acci=
dental closure retention</strong> in our event handlers. Specifically, we w=
ere creating event listeners inside React useEffect hooks that were inadver=
tently capturing large data structures in their lexical scope.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Here's a simplified version of t=
he problematic pattern we had:</p>
