">historicalData</code> array remained in memory because the event handler =
closure had captured it. Understanding <strong>V8's closure implementation<=
/strong> helped me identify that the entire lexical environment was being r=
etained, not just the variables we actually used.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Th=
at's a perfect example of closure-related memory leaks! And you're absolute=
ly right about V8 capturing the entire lexical environment. This tells me y=
ou have hands-on experience with the exact issues we're going to discuss to=
day.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Now, let's transition into the d=
eep technical discussion. I want to explore your understanding of <strong>h=
ow V8 actually implements closures at the engine level</strong>. This is cr=
ucial knowledge for senior engineers at NAB because we need to write code t=
hat's not just functional, but optimally performant.</p>
