<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">Real-World Impac=
t</h3>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">At scale, these optimizations ar=
e crucial. In my previous role, we had a data processing pipeline that crea=
ted thousands of closures for transform functions. Understanding these opti=
mizations helped us structure our code to work <strong>with</strong> V8's o=
ptimization strategies rather than against them.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Im=
pressive! You clearly understand the nuanced optimization strategies. Now, =
let's talk about a scenario that's very relevant to our work at NAB - <stro=
ng>memory management in long-running applications</strong>.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">We have web applications that ou=
r staff use for 8+ hours daily, handling constant streams of financial data=
. What are the specific <strong>memory risks</strong> with closures in such=
 environments, and how would you architect solutions to mitigate them?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: This=
 is absolutely critical for long-running applications like those at NAB. Le=
t me break down the <strong>primary memory risks</strong> and <strong>archi=
tectural solutions</strong>:</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">Critical Memory =
Risks</h3>
