al-time performance tracking and optimization recommendations</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The key insight is balancing the=
 <strong>functional programming benefits of closures</strong> with the <str=
ong>performance requirements of high-frequency financial data processing</s=
trong>. This architecture achieves both goals through careful optimization =
and resource management.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ex=
ceptional work! Your real-time event processing architecture demonstrates e=
xactly the kind of <strong>systems thinking</strong> and <strong>performanc=
e-oriented design</strong> we need at NAB. The adaptive memory management a=
nd performance monitoring components show you understand not just the techn=
ical implementation, but also the operational requirements of production sy=
stems.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Now, let's move to our final sec=
