<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Gr=
eat start! I like how you're using typed arrays for memory efficiency. Can =
you explain your decision to use <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border=
-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem]=
 px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Float64Array</code> and <code class=3D"bg-text-2=
00/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wra=
p rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Uint32Array</code>, and how th=
is helps with closure optimization?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Exce=
llent question! The typed array decision is crucial for both <strong>memory=
 efficiency</strong> and <strong>closure optimization</strong>:</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">Memory Efficienc=
y Benefits:</h3>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Predictable Memory Layo=
ut</strong>: Typed arrays allocate contiguous memory blocks, reducing fragm=
entation</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>No Object Overhead</str=
ong>: Regular JavaScript arrays have object metadata overhead - typed array=
s store raw binary data</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Cache Locality</strong>=
: Sequential memory access patterns improve CPU cache performance</li>
</ol>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">Closure Optimiza=
tion Benefits:</h3>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Monomorphic Access</str=
ong>: TurboFan can optimize typed array access more aggressively because th=
e types are guaranteed</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Eliminated Bounds Check=
ing</strong>: In optimized code, V8 can eliminate bounds checks for typed a=
rrays</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Reduced GC Pressure</st=
rong>: Fewer object allocations mean less garbage collection overhead</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me continue with the window =
aggregator implementation to show how this benefits closure compilation:</p=
